{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MEtXQKBdigvYC4UyCZu9eb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Murday Cotts 1968 liquid lithium self-diffusion D0 activation energy cm2/s spin echo\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"r m cotts 1Z8Qzy\",\"url\":\"https://scite.ai/authors/r-m-cotts-1Z8Qzy\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR\",\"url\":\"https://magritek.com/?p=21016\"},{\"title\":\"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/\"},{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"},{\"title\":\"s00231 011 0874 9\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9\"},{\"title\":\"subject:Self diffusion coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients\"},{\"title\":\"Self-Diffusion in Molten Lithium Nitrate\",\"url\":\"https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........d6d6807597b1fec9872b396fc4495643\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion in liquid lithium from coherent quasielastic neutron scattering\",\"url\":\"https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........2430b859cd2c8ede718b24c249f43fd0\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion and isotopic effects in liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scilit.com/publications/a87ad4db2680c466d4fc33f00ce090a5\"},{\"title\":\"next.sciencegate.app\",\"url\":\"https://next.sciencegate.app/document/10.1557/opl.2012.1517\"}]\n\nI ran one search, and it didn't return the D0 or activation-energy values from Murday and Cotts (1968). Here is what it did turn up:\n\n- **Citation confirmed:** A 2012 paper lists the reference as Murday JS, Cotts RM (1968) Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium. J Chem Phys 48:4938–4945.\n- **Method:** An abstract on a Cotts author page says the coefficient of self-diffusion of 7Li in liquid lithium has been measured with nuclear magnetic resonance, using the dependence of the spin-echo signal upon the amplitude of a pulsed magnetic field gradient. This abstract is not explicitly tied to the 1968 paper in the results, so treat that link as unconfirmed.\n- **Later comparison:** A 2012 simulation study reports that its calculated values are in good agreement with Murday's experiment results in atmosphere. It is a secondary source, so it does not give the 1968 D0 or Ea.\n\nTo get the actual numbers, check the J. Chem. Phys. 48, 4938 (1968) paper directly, or a review of liquid lithium diffusion data that tabulates it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a11176f-3086-43ac-8358-e42037899d12","uuid":"40920f97-c04c-42b4-a630-e6ecd3d01aa5","timestamp":"2026-11-01T08:53:43.634Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Murday Cotts 1968 liquid lithium self-diffusion D0 activation energy cm2/s spin echo","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019KUeAhJHE4tvHXk8pVx5kr","content":[{"title":"r m cotts 1Z8Qzy","url":"https://scite.ai/authors/r-m-cotts-1Z8Qzy"},{"title":"Self-diffusion coefficients of ionic liquids measured by multinuclear benchtop NMR","url":"https://magritek.com/?p=21016"},{"title":"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium","url":"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/"},{"title":"link.springer.com","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553"},{"title":"s00231 011 0874 9","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9"},{"title":"subject:Self diffusion coefficients","url":"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients"},{"title":"Self-Diffusion in Molten Lithium Nitrate","url":"https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........d6d6807597b1fec9872b396fc4495643"},{"title":"